## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design per-tenant secrets strategy, runtime access flow, rotation, and CI safety beyond data isolation.

## Key Concepts
- Secrets Manager per-tenant isolation
- Workload Identity for runtime retrieval
- CMEK-backed encryption and rotation
- CI gate validating cross-tenant access and rollback

## Code Example
```javascript
const {SecretManagerServiceClient} = require('@google-cloud/secret-manager');
const client = new SecretManagerServiceClient();
async function accessSecret(tenantId, suffix) {
  const name = `projects/${PROJECT_ID}/secrets/tenant-${tenantId}-${suffix}/versions/latest`;
  const [version] = await client.accessSecretVersion({name});
  return version.payload.data.toString('utf8');
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test rotation impact on live traffic?
- How would you revoke access for a suspended tenant?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests end-to-end thinking for tenant-scoped data retention across multiple services with auditability and rollback capabilities.

## Key Concepts

- Data tagging and lineage across Storage, BigQuery, and Pub/Sub
- Tenant-scoped retention policies, TTLs, and legal holds
- IAM Conditions, per-tenant service accounts, and KMS constraints
- Immutable logs and cryptographic attestations for verification
- Rollback procedures and audit verification planning

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-code for tenant deletion
function deleteTenant(tenantId) {
  purgePubSub(tenantId);
  deleteStorageObjects(tenantId);
  dropBigQueryPartitions(tenantId);
  verifyDeletion(tenantId);
  generateAuditReport(tenantId);
}
```
